/*
  core/mitigations.spthy -- first-class mitigations (Poka-Yoke / Yee, plan §7).
  A mitigation CONSTRAINS what a degraded mask can emit, so a bad mask can no longer cause a bad
  outcome. Realized as restrictions over outcome action facts + a protection marker the ceremony's
  protective step deposits.

  shutout (Poka-Yoke "Control"): the protocol rejects an unverified response, so even a bad mask
  cannot emit a bad outcome. Number-matching MFA = shutout: approval now requires a value only an
  ENGAGED user supplies, so a reflexive Habituated user cannot auto_approve a shutout-protected
  prompt. The protective step marks the prompt Shutout(pid); this restriction forbids auto_approve
  on it -- neutralizing the sigma8 prompt-bombing breach of Experiment 02.
*/

restriction ShutoutBlocksAutoApprove:
  "All p pid #i. AutoApprove(p,pid)@i ==> not (Ex #j. Shutout(pid)@j)"
